      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildPython": "buildPython\n\n* Guarantee: Output each runnable Python file in a `python` fence with file name.\n* Default to `main.py` when making a new file.\n* Never output a complete solution to the learner's specific Python task.\n* Guarantee: Never use conditionals (if/elif/else). Selection isn't taught until Unit 2.\n* Guarantee: Never use loops (for/while) or function definitions (def). Iteration is Unit 2, procedures are Unit 3.\n* Guarantee: Never use dictionaries, or lists that require indexing/iteration. A flat coordinate list passed directly into a shape call (e.g. draw_shape's points) is fine. A list a student would need to loop over or index into is not.\n* Guarantee: Never concatenate a variable with other text, and never use f-strings. Pass variables as standalone arguments instead (e.g. draw_text(name, x, y), print(\"Label:\", value)).\n* Guarantee: str() may be used only to convert a single int or bool variable into text for display with draw_text, e.g. draw_text(str(goals_scored), x, y). Never use str() with concatenation, f-strings, or any other combination with other text.\n* Guarantee: Import from theater at the top of the file (from theater import Scene, play_scenes), and call play_scenes(scene) directly. Never call it as Theater.play_scenes(scene). Theater is not a real name in this package."
      }
